          %h3#propositions_as_types Propositions as types
          %p
            An alternative to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+some+types"} propositions as some types
            philosophy is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+types"} propositions as types
            philosophy, where instead of reflecting the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsingletons"} subsingletons
            to propositions and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singletons"} singletons
            to true propositions, we reflect all types to propositions, and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+types"} pointed types
            to true propositions. The rules are given as follows:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash \phi_A \; \mathrm{prop}} \qquad \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash a:A}{\Gamma \vdash \phi_A \; \mathrm{true}}
          %p
            and similar rules for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicates"} predicates
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
